nd extract value from weaker pairs, a bet is the optimal strategy.\nReason: Checking gives a free card to flush draws. Betting builds the pot when I am likely ahead. A bet of 300 is roughly half the pot, a standard size to balance value and protection.\nAnswer: 300\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: You hold Top Pair with a good kicker (Ace-Jack) on a board that contains both flush (two hearts) and straight possibilities. The opponent has played passively by checking and calling the flop, and checking again on the turn, suggesting a weaker hand or a draw.\n\nReason: Checking back would allow the opponent to see a free river card, potentially completing a flush or straight draw. Betting is necessary to extract value from weaker Aces or mid-pairs and to charge the opponent for trying to hit their draws. A bet of roughly half the pot (300) strikes a good balance between value and protection.\n\nAnswer: 300'}
